1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,424
Don’t worry, my love.

2
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:51,801
I’ll take care of the children.

3
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,262
Rest now, my love.

4
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:56,514
We’ll see each other again.
Just wait for me.

5
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:57,432
Oh, Mom.

6
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,559
To the father of all of you.

7
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:08,068
Viktor and Donabel escaped!

8
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:10,320
That’s not even the bad news, yet.

9
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:14,657
We have reason to believe

10
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:17,869
that they’ve already left the country.

11
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:19,746
What?

12
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,292
You’re making the wrong decision.

13
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,336
Didn’t you two already plan
a life together?

14
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:27,253
What happened?

15
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:31,633
We all know there’s really no future
for Mikoy and me.

16
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:34,427
I can’t escape who I really am.

17
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,110
NORBERTO S. RUIZ
GENERAL

18
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,078
Mikoy.

19
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:02,956
Mikoy.

20
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:07,127
Mikoy, where are you going?

21
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:10,964
If I'm not mistaken,

22
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,967
I am no longer a police asset
of this agency.

23
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,597
You don't get to run my life anymore.

24
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:24,352
I understand what you're feeling.

25
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:28,064
Really?

26
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,360
You have no idea

27
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:34,988
what I'm going through.

28
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:43,538
Stop acting like you're the only one
who lost someone they loved.

29
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:45,915
You're not the only one who's hurting.

30
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:50,336
You're not the only one
who lost a family member.

31
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:54,382
And you're not the only one
who became a victim of injustice.

32
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:59,470
Look at what I did with myself.

33
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,641
I didn't wallow in self-pity.

34
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,478
I didn't let my anger consume me.

35
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,981
I entered the system,

36
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:13,151
and I tried to make the system work,

37
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:15,486
so I could get the justice
I was looking for.

38
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:18,698
Did you get it?

39
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:23,745
Did you get justice for your father?

40
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,373
Did you find the person who killed him?

41
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:33,004
Did you make the people who did this
to you and your family pay?

42
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:40,386
You're right.

43
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:42,764
I didn’t.

44
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,602
But every day that I do this,

45
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:48,895
I pray for just one thing.

46
00:03:49,395 --> 00:03:51,814
That no one else gets dragged into this,

47
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,942
that no one else has to experience

48
00:03:54,025 --> 00:03:56,444
the injustice that I experienced.

49
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,824
And I promised myself, Mikoy,

50
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:06,621
that I would never ever
take the law into my own hands.

51
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,707
Because that's not true justice.

52
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:13,419
It only spreads the same violence
even further,

53
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,672
the very violence that victimized
my father and my family.

54
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:19,509
So please, Mikoy,

55
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:22,345
don't do something
you'll regret in the end.

56
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,847
Yes, you're right.

57
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,518
Let's get justice for Dad Mario's death.

58
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:31,688
But let's do it the right way.

59
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,650
Because I'm sure

60
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:39,279
that's what he would want too.

61
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:04,012
Our top priority is figuring out
how to control the Concordat.

62
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:08,516
Yes, a lot of them have switched sides
and are supporting us,

63
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:11,269
but there are still many
who are fighting back.

64
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,938
Especially Rio de Janyx's faction.

65
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:24,949
What are you going to do?

66
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:27,702
I'm going back to the Philippines for now.

67
00:05:27,785 --> 00:05:31,372
To make sure Rahmboy
has cleaned up everything.

68
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,712
Don't tell me you're going to miss me.

69
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:44,802
There's just one more obstacle
to my leadership of the Concordat.

70
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:46,804
Who?

71
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:24,050
Move over.

72
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:25,468
Relax. Come on, come on.

73
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,470
Relax. We're not the enemy.

74
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:31,933
If you're not the enemy,
why are you following me?

75
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:33,184
What do you want?

76
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,811
Just a second.

77
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:36,104
I'm just getting my wallet.

78
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,313
I'm just getting my wallet.

79
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:38,606
Here, here.

80
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:47,740
BUREAU OF INTELLIGENCE
AND BLACK OPERATIONS

81
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:49,367
BIBO?

82
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:01,796
I think we're the ones
who can help with your problem.

83
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:04,298
Hey, not too fast.

84
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,552
What do you mean?

85
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:13,391
If you really want to get justice
for your father's death,

86
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,601
call me.

87
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:23,734
We're the agency

88
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,778
that operates in the shadows.

89
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:28,739
We're also the agency

90
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,784
that can bend the rules.

91
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:01,147
<i>Where are you?</i>

92
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:20,458
So you'd better tell me where you are.

93
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:33,638
And another thing, you are not a queen.

94
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:57,453
<i>So you think we’re still redeemable, huh?</i>

95
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:01,499
Between the two of us,
I thought I was the naive one.

96
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,293
But I guess I was wrong.

97
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,265
<i>And the more you hide,</i>

98
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,433
<i>the more reason you give me to believe</i>

99
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,227
that you're not on my side.

100
00:09:29,902 --> 00:09:32,947
Donatello, you won't beat me.

101
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,579
<i>So here's your only choice.</i>

102
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:44,000
Family, sibling, or whatever
you want to call it.

103
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:51,007
<i>Or I'll hunt you down myself.</i>

104
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:07,440
It can't be that I'm the only one
who's heartbroken in this story.

105
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:30,713
I'm on my way back.

106
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,965
Okay, we have a big problem.

107
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:34,342
What kind of problem?

108
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:57,990
<i>If you really want to get justice</i>
<i>for your father's death,</i>

109
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,367
<i>call me.</i>

110
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:03,204
<i>We're the agency</i>
<i>that can operate in the shadows.</i>

111
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:07,083
<i>We're also the agency</i>
<i>that can bend the rules.</i>

112
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:27,603
Mikoy?

113
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:47,873
Mikoy and I are getting married.

114
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:52,086
Looks like you learned a lot from Chiara.

115
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:03,639
Do you know all of this?

116
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:20,948
If there's one thing impressive about you,

117
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,075
it's your loyalty to her.

118
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:29,665
No one can stop me.

119
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:32,751
Until I get justice for my father's death.

120
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:36,422
<i>I don't care if all of you</i>
<i>and your minions join forces.</i>

121
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:39,008
Because I'll wipe you all out.

122
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,052
<i>Until people like you</i>
<i>no longer exist in this world.</i>

123
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,900
If you're going to kill me,
Chiara, or anyone else,

124
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:59,445
it won't make the pain
you're feeling go away.

125
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,742
<i>Before you go down this path, my friend,</i>

126
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,495
<i>is this really what you want?</i>

127
00:13:19,965 --> 00:13:21,884
The day she killed my father.

128
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:43,007
Hello, Mom?

129
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,258
<i>Hello, son, Mikoy.</i>

130
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:45,926
Where are you?

131
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,428
Don't you have work?

132
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:51,765
I do, Mom. I'm here in Manila.

133
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:52,808
What?

134
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,394
What are you doing there?

135
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:57,187
Is this because of your father?

136
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,481
No, Mom.

137
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:02,109
This isn't about Dad.

138
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:03,027
<i>Oh.</i>

139
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,863
<i>If not, why are you there</i>
<i>without telling me?</i>

140
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:09,116
Are you craving floods, son?

141
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:12,244
Pothole-filled roads and pollution?

142
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:13,954
Is that what you're looking for?

143
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:15,831
Come on, Mom.

144
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:18,375
Not all the roads here
are full of potholes.

145
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:21,420
<i>Besides, they're just a little bumpy.</i>

146
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:24,381
And it's not exactly pollution.

147
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,175
Can't it just be foggy, Mom?

148
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,178
Oh, you.

149
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:32,014
It's the same thing.
You just said it differently.

150
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,767
Don't try to dodge the question.

151
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:35,976
Why are you there?

152
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,812
I just had to take care of something

153
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,066
as a tourism officer in Albay.

154
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:45,235
<i>I'm joining a…</i>

155
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:46,654
<i>travel expo next month.</i>

156
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:49,198
I'm just going to showcase
the beauty of Albay.

157
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:52,284
We can't be the only ones
who get to see how beautiful it is, right?

158
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,787
<i>Mom.</i>

159
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:57,581
<i>Please believe me.</i>

160
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,583
I'm really okay.

161
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:03,796
And yes, I really am working here.

162
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:06,256
Okay, Mom?

163
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:41,000
What do you mean?

164
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:43,335
Just yesterday, he got
connected with BIBO.

165
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:45,963
Who are these BIBOs?

166
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:54,722
Their M.O. is simple.

167
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:02,771
And they operate off the record
and unofficially for the government.

168
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:06,066
Because with so many bad people,
criminals,

169
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,152
<i>the law can't keep up with all of them.</i>

170
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,863
<i>So because of their power and protection,</i>

171
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:12,114
this group was formed.

172
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,498
I'm just worried and afraid

173
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,959
that if they manage to get
Mikoy on their side,

174
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:26,295
Chiara won't be the only one in danger,

175
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:28,130
you won't be the only one in danger,

176
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:31,091
the whole squad will be in danger.

177
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:36,263
Chiara specifically instructed us
not to make a move against Mikoy.

178
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,932
If anything happens to Mikoy,

179
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:41,018
we'll be the ones who take the hit.

180
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:47,483
Unless you can make it
look like an accident.

181
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:11,840
<i>I don’t care</i>
<i>if it’s not fine or if it’s wrong.</i>

182
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:13,759
<i>All I know is that</i>

183
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:16,178
<i>I love you so much.</i>

184
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,597
<i>And it doesn’t matter</i>

185
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:20,974
<i>if the whole world is angry at you.</i>

186
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:23,894
<i>I will face them all for you.</i>

187
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:55,592
Seriously?

188
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:57,803
La Fornarina?

189
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,767
Asking someone to open a water bottle?

190
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:11,233
Even if I'm the infamous La Fornarina,

191
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,151
the deadliest,

192
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:14,736
most powerful assassin in the world,

193
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,446
I'm still a woman,

194
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,448
standing in front of a boy,

195
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:21,368
asking him to open my water bottle!

196
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:22,744
Or I will snap your neck

197
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:25,372
and send you to an early grave!

198
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:27,916
Okay, okay. Here, here.

199
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:28,959
I'm opening it.

200
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:31,628
Come on, sweetheart. Don't threaten me.

201
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:32,838
See? It's that easy.

202
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:34,631
- Exactly.
- Thank you, sweetheart.

203
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,010
Let me have a little.

204
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:04,870
I hope you're doing well.

205
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:13,378
<i>I hope you're eating properly, my love.</i>

206
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:19,092
And I hope

207
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:23,305
<i>you don't let your anger</i>
<i>consume you too much.</i>

208
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:57,297
Yes, yes.

209
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:22,614
Just finish your breakfast, you two.

210
00:21:23,198 --> 00:21:26,326
No, Cocoy and Carlota, you're still new
to the force, so you don't know.

211
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,412
But this is Janggo,

212
00:21:28,495 --> 00:21:32,207
from the Bureau of Intelligence
and Black Operations, or BIBO

213
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:35,210
Those people who work in the shadows.

214
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:44,303
All we offer is an additional tool
for the government

215
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:47,764
for dealing with criminals who have
escaped our justice system.

216
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:51,893
We don't neutralize people
just for the sake of neutralizing them.

217
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:55,314
We only do this when it's necessary
to make them pay for their crimes,

218
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,524
and to make sure
they can't hurt anyone again.

219
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:03,947
Is that what you tell yourself
to justify killings?

220
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:30,265
To get the justice I've been looking for?

221
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:45,489
Now it's up to you and the entire agency

222
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:47,240
whether you want to be part
of this decision.

223
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,371
She already victimized my father.

224
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:55,832
And I won't let that happen
to anyone else.

225
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:10,680
Even we are tired of this slow justice.

226
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:23,610
A true brother.

227
00:23:32,702 --> 00:23:34,412
But in our world,

228
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:38,792
BIBO is a legitimate agency,

229
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:40,418
and they are legal.

230
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:17,998
<i>From this moment on,</i>

231
00:24:31,094 --> 00:24:33,972
When Chiara took her seat
as the Queen of the Concordat,

232
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:36,141
<i>the organization regained its strength.</i>

233
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,310
All of their operations are in Europe.

234
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:40,228
But sooner or later,
they will reach the Philippines too.

235
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,605
And to prevent that from happening,

236
00:24:41,688 --> 00:24:43,148
we have to neutralize Chiara.

237
00:24:46,651 --> 00:24:48,153
Your mother respects you.

238
00:24:48,236 --> 00:24:51,364
But that doesn’t mean
I will extend that same courtesy to you.

239
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:54,409
What makes you say that?

240
00:24:54,492 --> 00:24:57,954
Because Bro Mikoy has one thing
that you don’t.

241
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:58,872
And what is that?

242
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:00,749
He has a reason to live.

243
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:05,086
Mikoy.

244
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:07,297
We have new information.
